#usda 1.0
(
    doc = """rover_01 mission: 5 named paths, 363.3 m, 939.0 s, with a pick-and-place transfer.

Cruise 0.5 m/s (0.25 m/s in the cross-aisle), accel 0.25 m/s^2, turns 30.0 deg/s. Velocity is profiled (forward/backward pass) so there are no instantaneous speed steps -- the chase camera is rigidly parented, so rover jerk is camera jerk.

IMPORTANT: these are time-sampled TRANSFORMS. Time-sampled transforms and PhysX articulation control are mutually exclusive -- press Play with the articulation active and PhysX drives the robot, ignoring this. Use this layer for SDG capture, flythroughs and deterministic replay. To drive the same route under physics, feed scenario/routes.usda to a controller and mute this layer. tote_payload is authored KINEMATIC so its scripted motion is authoritative while it still collides."""
    kilogramsPerUnit = 1
    metersPerUnit = 1
    timeCodesPerSecond = 60
    upAxis = "Z"
)

